  "worked_solution": "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. A square is a rectangle where all sides are congruent, hence $AB=BC=CD=AD.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The angles in a square are all right. Therefore, $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}=m∠ADC.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Opposite sides of a square are parallel, and $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is opposite $\\overset{―}{BC},$ therefore $\\overset{―}{AD}$ is parallel to $\\overset{―}{BC}.$\n\nIn conclusion, statements I, II, and III are true.",
